9. Quick Revision Cheat Sheet
Boosting = sequential trees fitting the negative gradient of the loss; bagging = parallel trees for variance.
Prediction update: F_m = F_{m-1} + η·h_m.
Small learning_rate + many trees + early stopping is the standard recipe.
XGBoost = reliable, LightGBM = fast (watch num_leaves), CatBoost = best categoricals/defaults.
Imbalance: scale_pos_weight = neg/pos, or SMOTE inside the training fold.
Regularize with depth, min_child_weight, subsample, colsample, L1/L2.
Tuning order: LR/trees → structure → sampling → regularization → lower LR.
RandomSearch beats Grid; Optuna beats Random on bigger spaces; nested CV gives honest estimates.
Good AUC does not mean good probabilities. Check calibration (reliability curve + Brier).
Calibrate with sigmoid (small data) or isotonic (large data) on unseen data, then tune the threshold.
Never early-stop or tune on the test set. Always keep a baseline.
